This project is an independent ZCode implementation inspired by:

- pstack, https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
  Copyright Cursor, MIT License. Original skill set and workflow design by Lauren Tan.
- open-pstack, https://github.com/ericlitman/open-pstack
  Copyright Eric Litman, MIT License. Verification-skill architecture and the
  exact-head evidence model.
- ponytail, https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail
  Copyright Dietrich Gebert, MIT License. The necessity ladder, the
  over-engineering review rubric, the audit report structure, and the
  "shortcut:" comment convention used by kelin-refine and kelin-audit.

No upstream source file is copied verbatim. The skill text, scripts, tests and
verification harness in this repository were written for ZCode and translated
into Chinese. Shared ideas: the plan/verify/review/ship workflow split, the
"proof over claims" verification stance, the feature-map plus recipe structure
used by the verifier, and the minimal-code ladder adapted for kelin-refine.
